Sheoldred does both halves of a sacrifice deck at once: she reanimates a creature for free on your upkeep, and she makes every opponent sacrifice one on theirs. So the deck is built out of creatures that WANT to die — Kokusho, Junji, Archon of Cruelty — and outlets to kill them on your own terms. Bring one back every turn, cash it in for value, repeat.

# The commander
Sheoldred, Whispering One :: 6/6 with swampwalk, a free reanimation every one of your upkeeps, and a forced sacrifice on every opponent's upkeep. Seven mana, and she is worth every one of them.
Lightning Greaves :: shroud, because she is the single most removal-magnetic card in the deck.
Swiftfoot Boots :: hexproof and haste for when you want to attack immediately.
Kaya's Ghostform :: one mana that brings her back through destruction OR exile.
Imp's Mischief :: redirects the removal spell aimed at her.

# Creatures that pay you for dying
Kokusho, the Evening Star :: five life from each opponent and fifteen back to you, every time it dies. Reanimate it on upkeep, sacrifice it, repeat — that is fifteen damage a turn cycle in a four-player pod.
Junji, the Midnight Sky :: two cards discarded and two life from each opponent, or it reanimates something else on its way out.
Archon of Cruelty :: a sacrifice, a discard and three life from an opponent when it ENTERS, so Sheoldred's upkeep trigger alone is a beating, and it triggers again on every attack.
Grave Titan :: six power and four Zombies across entry and attack, all of them sacrifice fodder.
Massacre Wurm :: a one-sided wrath on entry, and every creature they lose costs two life.
Gray Merchant of Asphodel :: your devotion is high; reanimating it is six or more damage to each opponent.
Sephiroth, Fabled SOLDIER :: draws off every sacrifice, drains on every creature death, and flips into an emblem that keeps draining for the rest of the game.

# Sacrifice outlets
Ashnod's Altar :: free, repeatable, and it makes mana. This is what turns Sheoldred's reanimation into a loop.
Deadly Dispute :: two cards and a Treasure for a creature you were going to lose anyway.
Skullclamp :: on a 2/2 Zombie, two cards.
Braids, Arisen Nightmare :: every end step they give up a permanent or you draw and they lose two.
Gate to Phyrexia :: repeatable artifact removal that costs only a body.
Sephiroth, Fabled SOLDIER :: a free sacrifice on entry and every attack, each one a card.

# Punishing the deaths
Grave Pact :: every creature you lose makes each opponent sacrifice one. Alongside Sheoldred's upkeep edict, the table simply cannot keep a board.
Syr Konrad, the Grim :: damage to each opponent whenever a creature dies anywhere, whenever a creature card is milled or discarded, AND whenever a creature card leaves your graveyard — so Sheoldred's reanimation trigger itself pings the table every upkeep.
Morbid Opportunist :: a card every turn creatures die.
Accursed Marauder :: everyone sacrifices a nontoken creature. You have fodder; they usually do not.
Plaguecrafter :: the same, and it catches planeswalkers.
Emeritus of Woe :: a 5/4 that also carries a Demonic Tutor, and it re-prepares whenever two creatures die in a turn.

# Getting the fatties down there
Entomb :: one mana, instant speed, exactly what you want.
Buried Alive :: three at once. Kokusho, Archon of Cruelty and Junji is the standard pile.
Perpetual Timepiece :: mills two at a time, and shuffles back in when you are at risk of decking.
Grave Researcher :: surveils each upkeep and prepares a free Reanimate once three creatures are down.
Reanimate :: one mana for anything in any graveyard.
Animate Dead :: the second copy.
Necromancy :: flash speed, so you can rebuild in response to a wrath.
Living Death :: your graveyard is the deepest at the table by design.
Phyrexian Reclamation :: buys creatures back to your HAND, which matters when they exile your graveyard.

# Removal and interaction
Deadly Rollick :: free with your commander out.
Bitter Triumph :: a creature or planeswalker, and the discard cost puts a fatty where you want it.
Feed the Swarm :: mono-black's only clean enchantment answer.
Meteor Golem :: destroys any nonland permanent, and it is a creature so Sheoldred can rebuy it.
Gate to Phyrexia :: artifacts, repeatedly.
Liquimetal Torque :: turns any permanent into an artifact so the Gate can eat it.
Opposition Agent :: flash him onto a fetchland or tutor.
Stonespeaker Crystal :: mana, and it exiles graveyards while drawing you a card — useful when someone else is the reanimator.

# Mana and cards
Sol Ring :: turn one.
Jet Medallion :: a discount on every card in the deck.
Crypt Ghast :: doubles every Swamp and extorts on every spell.
Mind Stone :: ramp early, a card later.
Black Market Connections :: three effects a turn.
Night's Whisper :: two cards for two mana.
Solemn Simulacrum :: a land, a card, and a body to sacrifice.
Expedition Map :: finds Cabal Coffers or whichever land the board needs.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep a graveyard enabler and acceleration. Entomb plus Reanimate is a turn-two Archon of Cruelty, which is faster than casting Sheoldred and better than waiting for her.
Sheoldred is a seven-drop. Crypt Ghast, Sol Ring and Jet Medallion are what make her a turn-five play. Do not keep a hand that only works if you draw four more lands.
Sacrifice on your upkeep, not your main phase. Sheoldred's trigger reanimates first — so put Kokusho back, then sacrifice it during your turn, then do it again next upkeep. Killing it before the trigger wastes a whole turn of value.
Grave Pact :: with Sheoldred out this is the lock. Their upkeep edict plus your sacrifice outlet means every opponent loses two creatures per turn cycle and cannot rebuild.
